      "limits": "⚠ Limits",
      "linguistic_bias": "Linguistic bias",
      "linkedin_desc": "6 sections: what recruiters actually look at, photo + banner, headline + About, experience section, engagement (the underrated lever), active job-search mode + Premium worth it?",
      "listen_carefully_repeat_the_sentence_e": "Listen carefully + repeat the sentence exactly.",
      "listen_then_repeat_the_digits_in_rever": "Listen, then repeat the digits in REVERSE order.",
      "listen_then_repeat_the_digits_in_the_s": "Listen, then repeat the digits in the same order.",
      "listen_then_say_all_the_numbers_in_ord": "Listen, then say all the numbers in order first, then all the letters in order.",
      "listen_to_sounds_blend_them_into_a_wor": "Listen to sounds; blend them into a word.",
      "listen_to_word_pairs_after_all_pairs_a": "Listen to word pairs. After all pairs are read, you'll be asked to recall.",
      "low_scores_can_come_from_many_sources_": "low scores can come from many sources — knowing the narrow construct + sample task helps identify whether weakness is genuine, instructional gap, attention, anxiety, or accommodation issue.",
      "luria_s_functional_units": "Luria's Functional Units",
      "maine_desc": "AlloFlow flagship state. Higher ed, workforce development, vocational rehab + disability services, mental health resources, Maine-specific industries (lobstering, aquaculture, forestry, healthcare, composites), and Maine context for career planning.",
      "mark_yes_or_no_for_each_row_as_fast_as": "Mark \"yes\" or \"no\" for each row as fast as possible. 2 minutes.",
      "meaning_desc": "5 sections: what meaningful work means (3 dimensions), sources of meaning (different for different people), signs of values mismatch, mastery + craft as meaning source, integrating values into career decisions. Beyond money + status + interest fit.",
      "mentoring_desc": "5 sections: mentor vs sponsor (critical distinction), finding them, being a good mentee, becoming a mentor yourself, sponsorship dynamics. Research shows mentees + sponsored people advance faster + earn more. Worth investing in deliberately.",
      "mhfa_desc": "5 sections: ALGEE framework (Assess, Listen, Give reassurance, Encourage professional help, Encourage self-help), mental health crisis response, suicide risk assessment, youth-specific MHFA, crisis lines + resources. The non-clinical \"first aid\" for psychological distress.",
      "module_by_module_learning_objectives": "🎯 Module-by-Module Learning Objectives",
      "most_k_12_cases_do_not_require_neurops": "Most K-12 cases do NOT require neuropsych referral. Standard psychoed eval handles SLD, OHI (including ADHD), ID, SLI, and typical ASD presentations well. Reserve neuropsych referrals for: acquired brain injury (TBI with cognitive consequences), neurological conditions with cognitive implications (epilepsy, brain tumor, MS, cerebral palsy), complex atypical profiles that don't fit standard categories, cases where medical or legal decisions depend on comprehensive cognitive documentation. When referring, provide the neuropsychologist your comprehensive eval so they can build on it rather than duplicate.",
      "move_four_sliders_instrument_reliabili": "Move four sliders (instrument reliability, SEM, observed score, decision stakes). Predict the confidence interval width and the action-readiness of the score. No score, no reveal — you mark your own understanding.",
      "my_kid_s_iq_went_up_may_be_test_artifa": "\"My kid's IQ went up\" may be test artifact. ",
      "name_all_colors_in_order_as_fast_as_po": "Name all colors in order as fast as possible. Time + errors recorded.",
      "narrow_level_diagnosis_tells_you_which": "narrow-level diagnosis tells you which sub-skill to target. \"Reading weakness\" is vague; \"phonological awareness deficit\" (Ga: PC) or \"rapid naming deficit\" (Glr: NA) tell you what to do.",
      "negotiate_desc": "Evidence-based guide: 6 deep sections (overview + research / market data / word-for-word scripts / common mistakes / career-stage scenarios / equity comp). Worth $500K-$1.5M over a career when applied consistently. Drawn from Linda Babcock's research + contemporary US hiring reality.",
      "network_desc": "Visualize how careers connect. Pick a root career, see its neighborhood as an SVG network, click any node to traverse the web.",
      "neuropsychological_assessment_extends_": "Neuropsychological assessment extends beyond cognitive ability (g, CHC) into the specific brain-behavior relationships that matter after brain injury, in neurological conditions, or for atypical cognitive profiles standard batteries miss. Most school psychologists aren't neuropsychologists, but should recognize when to refer and what a neuropsych eval adds.",
      "neuropsychologically_grounded_derives_": "Neuropsychologically grounded — derives from Luria's work on brain function. Four components. Operationalized in the Cognitive Assessment System (CAS2). Strong for identifying specific cognitive deficits tied to neurological function.",
      "neuropsychology": "Neuropsychology",
